# Node packages, installed from package.json. Test and build dependencies of the
# factory, never something a demo loads, so they stay out of a repository whose
# whole job is to be served as static files.
#
# THE LOCKFILE IS COMMITTED, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF IT. There is a package.json
# now because there deliberately was not one before, and the absence had a cost:
# with no manifest, every install was --no-save, and npm treats a --no-save
# install as the complete intended contents of node_modules, pruning whatever the
# command did not name. Two install steps in the build workflow removed each
# other's packages in turn, and the failure surfaced three steps later inside a
# test about photographs. A manifest plus a lockfile plus npm ci is the shape
# where that cannot happen.
node_modules/
